  "system": {
    "description": "Despite the extreme temperatures of the solar corona, the plasma in that part of the sun's atmosphere is incredibly diffuse, meaning actual heat transfer is quite low, making it survivable with the right protections. Suryas blur the line between biomorph and synthmorph and push the envelope of synthetic biology in order to survive in this hostile environment. Named for a Hindu sun deity, suryas reach lengths of ten meters or more and rely heavily on both whale and extremophile genetics.",
